# ---- project: large or regenerable artifacts ----
# Snapshots are regenerable via Scripts/export_snapshots.py.
# Comment the next line out if you want to commit the snapshot set
# as part of the replication package (recommended for archival).
# data/snapshots/

# QLSQ skew-calibration cache -- regenerable via
# Scripts/skew_calibrate_{systematic,idiosyncratic}.py. Kept out of the
# repo because (a) it can be large as the sample window grows, and (b)
# calibration is deterministic given the code + market data so the cache
# is redundant with a reproducibility harness.
Study/Estimated Parameters QLSQ/*.parquet
Study/Estimated Parameters QLSQ/*.pkl
Study/Estimated Parameters QLSQ/*.csv

# scratch / exploratory notebooks (keep out of the replication package)
scratch_pad.ipynb
Scripts/test.ipynb

# ---- large regenerable Monte Carlo / P&L outputs ----
# These are ~130MB per file and are regenerated by running
# report_collar_asian.py. Keep them out of the repo.
Study/Collar Asian/final_output_*.csv
Study/Collar Asian/CurrentPV/
Study/Collar Asian/ScenarioPV/
